# Gurugram city page + 6 route pages (written 2026-11-22). Plain text only; rendered by gen_city_routes.py.
CITY = dict(
  name="Gurugram",
  intro="1st VRL works as packers and movers in Gurugram for flats, builder floors, offices, cars and bikes, both inside the city and on long routes across India. A verified partner team does the packing and loading here, while one coordinator at our Panchkula head office handles the survey, the written estimate and the GST bill from start to finish.",
  local="Moving out of a Gurugram tower is rarely about the stairs and nearly always about the rules. Most condominiums on Golf Course Extension Road, Sohna Road and the Dwarka Expressway want a move-out gate pass from the facility office, a clearance that maintenance dues are paid and a fixed slot on the service lift, and several ask for a refundable deposit that is returned after a check of the lift and lobby. Older parts of the city are different again: builder floors in Sushant Lok, South City and Palam Vihar often have a narrow staircase and a lift too small for a sofa, and the villages behind MG Road have lanes where a big truck cannot turn. In July and August heavy rain can flood stretches of NH48 and low roads within an hour, so monsoon loading is planned around the weather forecast.",
  how="Before the survey we ask for the society's move rules in writing, because they decide the date as much as the truck does. For DLF Phase 5, Golf Course Road and the Golf Course Extension towers, the partner team brings lift padding and floor sheets and works inside the slot the facility office gives. In Sushant Lok, South City and the HUDA sectors of old Gurugram, wardrobes and beds are often taken apart upstairs and carried down by hand. Around Chakkarpur, Sikanderpur and Nathupur, a small tempo shuttles cartons to a truck parked on the wider road. New Gurugram sectors along the Dwarka Expressway usually have wide approach roads but strict move hours, which we note on the plan.",
  areas=["DLF Phase 1","DLF Phase 2","DLF Phase 3","DLF Phase 4","DLF Phase 5","Golf Course Road","Golf Course Extension Road","Sohna Road","Sushant Lok","South City","Palam Vihar","Dwarka Expressway","New Gurugram","Nirvana Country","MG Road","Sector 14","Sector 56","Udyog Vihar","Manesar","Sohna"],
  photos=["sp/sp-team-truck-1200", "crew/crew-carton-shoulder", "crew/crew-wrapped-furniture", "crew/crew-carton-taping"],
  more=[
   ("Home shifting in Gurugram: a guide by area", [
     "Each part of the city brings its own kind of move. Packers and movers in DLF Phase 1 to 4 deal with a mix of independent houses and builder floors, so the crew count matters more than the truck size. In DLF Phase 5 and along Golf Course Road most homes are in tall condominium towers, where the service lift slot is the real deadline. Families leaving Sushant Lok or South City usually come from third or fourth floors with tight landings, and a large L-shaped sofa may need to be opened up at the joints before it goes down.",
     "Packers and movers in Palam Vihar and the sectors around it often have a quieter job, with lower floors and wider roads, but parking for the truck still has to be agreed with neighbours. The newer sectors along the Dwarka Expressway and in New Gurugram are mostly gated high-rises with good roads and long walks from the tower to the gate, so trolleys are sent for cartons. Old Gurugram villages such as Chakkarpur, Sikanderpur and Nathupur house many single professionals in rented rooms, and those moves are usually one room and a bike."]),
   ("Gurugram shifting charges for local moves", [
     "A move within Gurugram, or between Gurugram and Delhi or Faridabad, is priced on the local band of our house chart, because all three are treated as one metro. Under the same rule, short moves to Manesar and Sohna, which are in Gurugram district, are local too. On that band a 1 RK costs about Rs 3,000 to 6,500, a 1 BHK about Rs 5,000 to 9,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 8,000 to 15,000 and a 3 BHK about Rs 12,000 to 21,000, all plus GST. A 4 BHK or a large villa is about Rs 17,000 to 29,000 plus GST.",
     "Moves from Gurugram to Noida, Greater Noida or Ghaziabad are priced only after the survey, so we do not give a figure for them here. For longer trips the chart changes band by road distance: Chandigarh or Jaipur is in the up to 500 km band, Mumbai and Pune in the 500 to 1,500 km band, and Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Chennai and Kolkata in the 1,500 km plus band. A lift that is out of order or a long carry from the gate is shown as a separate line on the estimate, never added later."]),
   ("Corporate transfers and office shifting in Gurugram", [
     "A large share of moves out of Gurugram are job transfers. Staff from IT, consulting and MNC offices in Cyber City, Udyog Vihar and Golf Course Road are often moving on a joining date set by the new employer, and the company may be paying. In that case the GST invoice can be raised in the company's name with its GSTIN, and packing, transport and transit insurance are shown as separate lines so the finance team can approve it without calling us. When a company asks for comparison quotes, the written estimate follows a video survey, so no home visit is needed to get a figure.",
     "Office shifting in Gurugram is planned around working hours. A small office of up to 10 workstations moving within the city costs about Rs 12,000 to 25,000 plus GST, and a medium office of 10 to 30 workstations about Rs 25,000 to 60,000 plus GST. Business parks normally allow goods movement only after office hours or on weekends, with a permit from the building management, so the partner team packs desks and files on a Friday evening and sets them up before Monday. Dismantling and refitting a workstation is billed at Rs 800 to 2,000 per desk."]),
   ("Weather, timing and paperwork for a Gurugram move", [
     "The calendar changes how a Gurugram move goes. From May to mid June afternoons are very hot, so loading starts early and wooden furniture is kept away from direct sun. In July and August a heavy shower can flood stretches of NH48 and many internal roads in a short time, so cartons are sealed with extra tape, mattresses are wrapped in plastic and the truck is kept on higher ground. In December and January fog slows the highways at night, which can add a day to long routes heading north or east.",
     "Keep a few papers ready before the packing day. The society gate pass and the lift booking come first, then a copy of your ID and the new address for the transport documents. Tenants should collect the deposit settlement from the landlord before the truck leaves, because it is hard to chase from another city. If a car is going on a carrier, keep copies of the registration certificate and insurance ready for the inventory list, and if storage is needed between homes, it can be arranged through a partner warehouse, charged separately and shown on the estimate."]),
  ],
  faqs=[
   ("Is a move from Gurugram to Delhi charged as local?","Yes. Gurugram and Delhi are priced on the local band of the house chart, because they are treated as one metro. A 1 BHK costs about Rs 5,000 to 9,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 8,000 to 15,000 and a 3 BHK about Rs 12,000 to 21,000, plus GST. Delivery timing at the Delhi end follows the goods vehicle entry rules for that road."),
   ("What about Gurugram to Faridabad, Manesar or Sohna?","All three are also on the local band. Faridabad comes under the same metro rule as Delhi, and Manesar and Sohna are short moves inside Gurugram district. A 2 BHK costs about Rs 8,000 to 15,000 plus GST on this band, with any extra floors or long carries shown as their own line on the estimate."),
   ("Do you have an office in Gurugram?","No. In Gurugram the move is done by a verified partner team, and one coordinator from our head office at #705, Sector-7, Panchkula looks after the survey, the estimate, the schedule and your calls. The estimate and the GST invoice carry our name and GSTIN."),
   ("My society needs a lift booking and a deposit. Can you help?","Yes. Share the facility office rules with the coordinator once you have them. The partner team arrives inside the lift slot, pads the service lift and protects the lobby floor, which helps you get the deposit back. If the society allows moves only on weekdays, we plan the date around that first."),
   ("How much does it cost to shift from Gurugram to Noida?","Moves between Gurugram and Noida, Greater Noida or Ghaziabad are quoted only after a survey, because the price depends on the exact addresses and the route across Delhi. Call the 24-hour line, share both addresses and a rough list of goods, and you will get a written figure plus GST."),
   ("Can my employer pay for the move directly?","Yes. The invoice can be raised in your company's name with its GSTIN, and packing, transport and insurance are shown on separate lines. Many companies also want the estimate before approval, so we send it in writing after the survey."),
   ("Is it a problem to shift during the Gurugram monsoon?","It can be done safely with planning. We watch the forecast, avoid loading during a heavy spell, wrap mattresses and sofas in plastic and seal every carton with extra tape. If roads near your tower are known to flood, the truck waits on a dry stretch and goods are carried a little further."),
  ],
  routes=[
   dict(key="bengaluru", to="Bengaluru", km=2130, days="7 to 9 days", road="NH44",
    intro="This is one of the busiest job-change routes out of the NCR, carrying engineers, product managers and their families from Gurugram's tech offices to Bengaluru's.",
    about="The truck does not need to enter Delhi. It leaves Gurugram on the KMP Expressway towards Palwal, joins NH44 there and runs south past Mathura and Agra, through Gwalior and Jhansi, across Madhya Pradesh to Nagpur, and on through Adilabad to Hyderabad. From there it continues through Kurnool and Anantapur before entering Bengaluru from the north near Hebbal. At about 2,130 km this move is in the 1,500 km plus band, the top band on our chart. A shared truck normally delivers in 7 to 9 days from loading.",
    dest="Bengaluru apartments look a lot like Gurugram towers, so the move-in rules feel familiar: a form for the association office, a copy of the rental agreement, a lift slot and fixed move hours. The difference is traffic. Large trucks are restricted on many city roads at busy times, and the Outer Ring Road around Marathahalli and Bellandur can hold a truck for hours, so unloading is usually set for early morning. Bengaluru also gets rain for much of the year, with the heaviest spells from June to October, so a plastic sheet for the tower entrance travels with the goods.",
    tip="Ask your new Bengaluru society for its move-in form before the truck leaves Gurugram. Many associations take two or three working days to approve a slot, and the truck should not reach your gate before that approval does.",
    faqs=[("How long does shifting from Gurugram to Bengaluru take?","On a shared truck, 7 to 9 days from the loading day. A dedicated vehicle is faster but costs more. In December and January fog between Agra and Gwalior can add a day, and the coordinator tells you as soon as the plan changes."),
          ("Can I send my car from Gurugram to Bengaluru?","Yes, on a car carrier. A hatchback costs about Rs 13,000 to 22,000, a sedan about Rs 15,000 to 25,000, a compact SUV about Rs 17,000 to 28,000 and an SUV or MUV about Rs 20,000 to 34,000, plus GST. The car's condition is photographed at pickup."),
          ("Will my company accept your invoice for a Bengaluru transfer?","Usually yes. The GST invoice can carry your employer's name and GSTIN, with packing, transport and insurance listed separately. If the HR team has its own format for quotes, send it to us and we fill the estimate in that format.")],
    photos=["crew/crew-mattress-corrugated", "crew/crew-carton-shoulder", "crew/crew-wrapped-furniture", "crew/crew-carton-taping"],
    more=[
     ("Who moves from Gurugram to Bengaluru", [
       "Most bookings on this route are tied to a job. A software engineer leaves a Cyber City office for a product company in Whitefield, a consultant is posted to a client in Electronic City, or a couple both find roles on the Outer Ring Road and decide to move together. These moves usually come with a fixed joining date and a relocation budget, so the estimate has to be in writing early and the delivery window has to be realistic. Families also move for schools and for Bengaluru's milder weather after years of Gurugram summers.",
       "A typical load is a 2 BHK or 3 BHK from a tower on Golf Course Extension Road or Sohna Road, often with a home office setup, a large television and one car. Single professionals moving from rented rooms in Sector 56 or the villages behind MG Road usually send a 1 RK load with a bike. For Gurugram to Bengaluru packers and movers, both kinds of move use the same 1,500 km plus chart, and the survey decides where in the band your move sits."]),
     ("Packing a Gurugram home for a 2,100 km trip", [
       "Goods spend a week or more on the road, passing through dry heat in the north and humid weather in the south. Electronics such as monitors, routers and speakers are packed in their own cartons with foam, and laptops and documents should travel with you on the flight. Wooden furniture is wrapped in corrugated sheet and then stretch film, so that dust from the highway and dampness in Bengaluru do not reach the polish. Glass table tops are crated or packed between boards.",
       "Kitchen items are packed in double-walled cartons with paper between plates, and liquids such as oil and cleaning products should be used up or given away before the move, since a leak can spoil a whole carton. Potted plants rarely survive a week in a closed truck, so they are better given to neighbours. Every carton is numbered and listed on the inventory sheet, and you sign the same sheet when the Bengaluru partner team unloads, so a missing box shows up at once rather than weeks later."]),
     ("Gurugram to Bengaluru shifting charges, worked out", [
       "On the 1,500 km plus band, a 1 BHK from Gurugram to Bengaluru costs about Rs 20,000 to 35,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 27,000 to 47,000 and a 3 BHK about Rs 34,000 to 60,000, plus GST. A 4 BHK or a large villa is about Rs 44,000 to 78,000 plus GST. A Royal Enfield or similar bike from 150cc to 350cc adds about Rs 7,000 to 10,000 plus GST. Tolls, a lift that is not working and any storage at the Bengaluru end are shown as separate lines on the estimate, so the final bill matches what you approved."])]),
   dict(key="mumbai", to="Mumbai", km=1390, days="5 to 7 days", road="NH48 / Delhi-Mumbai Expressway",
    intro="This route mostly carries finance, media and consulting staff between the NCR's corporate hub and India's financial capital, plus families moving closer to relatives on the west coast.",
    about="Gurugram has an easy start to this trip because the Delhi-Mumbai Expressway begins near Sohna, inside Gurugram district. Depending on load and timing, the driver uses the open sections of that expressway or the older NH48 through Jaipur, Ajmer, Udaipur and Ahmedabad, and both routes meet again in Gujarat near Vadodara before the run south past Surat and Vapi into Mumbai. The road distance is about 1,390 km, so this move is in the 500 to 1,500 km band, the middle band of our chart. A shared truck usually takes 5 to 7 days.",
    dest="Most people moving from Gurugram to Mumbai lose space. A spacious 3 BHK on Golf Course Road often becomes a 2 BHK in Powai, Andheri or Thane, so deciding what to sell or store before the survey saves money. Before the truck is allowed in, a Mumbai housing society normally expects a letter from its secretary approving the move, and many fix the hours for shifting. Lifts in older buildings can be too small for a wardrobe, which is then taken apart. From June to September the rain is heavy and steady, so the unloading plan includes covers for the building entrance and the lift.",
    tip="Send us the inside measurements of your Mumbai lift and main door before packing starts in Gurugram. If the bed or sofa will not fit, it is taken apart at loading, which is far easier than on a crowded Mumbai landing.",
    faqs=[("How many days does Gurugram to Mumbai shifting take?","Usually 5 to 7 days on a shared truck from the day of loading, and less on a dedicated vehicle. The expected delivery date is on the estimate, and the Mumbai partner team calls before reaching your building."),
          ("Can you deliver to Navi Mumbai or Thane instead?","Yes. Thane, Navi Mumbai nodes such as Kharghar, Vashi and Nerul, and the western suburbs are all delivered on the same 500 to 1,500 km chart. Tell us the society's move-in rules early, because some ask for a few days' notice."),
          ("What does a bike cost from Gurugram to Mumbai?","A scooter costs about Rs 3,500 to 5,500, a bike up to 150cc about Rs 4,000 to 6,000, a 150cc to 350cc bike about Rs 5,500 to 8,000 and a premium bike above 350cc about Rs 8,000 to 11,500 on this route, plus GST.")],
    photos=["sp/sp-loading-720", "crew/crew-mattress-corrugated", "crew/crew-carton-shoulder", "crew/crew-wrapped-furniture"],
    more=[
     ("Why people shift from Gurugram to Mumbai", [
       "Banks, brokerages, advertising agencies and film and media companies pull a steady stream of Gurugram professionals to Mumbai. Many are moving from offices in Cyber City or on Golf Course Road to Lower Parel, BKC or Andheri, often on a transfer within the same company. Others are returning families who grew up in Maharashtra or Gujarat and want to be nearer home. Because rents in Mumbai are high, a lot of these moves also involve storing part of the household or selling furniture before leaving.",
       "Home shifting from Gurugram to Mumbai is easier when the new flat is fixed before the survey. With the floor plan in hand, the surveyor can tell you which pieces will fit, which should be dismantled and which might be better sold in Gurugram. That one conversation often moves a load from a 3 BHK estimate to a 2 BHK estimate, which is a real saving on the 500 to 1,500 km band. It also means fewer pieces to unload into a building where the lift is shared with every other flat."]),
     ("Packing for a west coast monsoon", [
       "If your move falls between June and September, assume that the goods will be unloaded in rain. Mattresses go into thick plastic covers, sofas and beds are wrapped in corrugated sheet and stretch film, and cartons with clothes or books are lined with plastic before sealing. Steel almirahs and appliances get an extra layer at the corners, because damp and scratches together lead to rust. Shoe racks and kitchen trolleys with metal frames get the same treatment.",
       "Outside the monsoon the bigger risk is the sheer number of floors and corridors at the Mumbai end. Pieces are labelled by room so the unloading team can take each one straight to the right place without leaving it in a narrow passage. Fragile items such as dinner sets, mirrors and photo frames are packed in separate marked cartons, and the inventory sheet shows them so you can open and check those first. Heavy cartons of books are kept small, because they are often carried by hand along long corridors in Mumbai buildings."]),
     ("Gurugram to Mumbai shifting charges and vehicles", [
       "For about 1,390 km, a 1 RK from Gurugram to Mumbai costs about Rs 13,000 to 23,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 20,000 to 36,000 and a 3 BHK about Rs 26,000 to 46,000, all plus GST. A sedan on a carrier costs about Rs 10,500 to 17,000 plus GST and an SUV or MUV about Rs 14,000 to 22,000 plus GST, while a luxury car in an enclosed carrier is about Rs 28,000 to 45,000 plus GST. Since Mumbai parking is tight, the car can be delivered to your building on a separate day if that suits the society better."])]),
   dict(key="pune", to="Pune", km=1430, days="5 to 7 days", road="Via Jaipur, Kota, Indore and Nashik",
    intro="Most moves on this route are IT and automotive staff heading to Hinjewadi, Kharadi and Chakan, and families choosing Pune for its weather, schools and calmer pace.",
    about="Leaving Gurugram, the truck takes NH48 towards Jaipur, then turns south through Kota and across Madhya Pradesh to Indore. From Indore the old Agra-Mumbai road heads down to the Narmada crossing at Khalghat and on to Dhule in Maharashtra, after which the driver takes the Nashik road and the Nashik-Pune highway through Sangamner into Pune. The road distance is about 1,430 km, which keeps this move in the 500 to 1,500 km band, the middle band on our chart. Household goods on a shared truck usually reach in 5 to 7 days.",
    dest="Pune has a lot of new high-rise societies in Hinjewadi, Wakad, Baner, Kharadi and Wagholi, and like Gurugram's towers they ask for a move-in form, a security pass for the truck and a booked lift. Traffic around the Hinjewadi IT park and on the Hadapsar side is heavy at office hours, so trucks are normally unloaded mid-morning or late in the evening. The monsoon from June to September brings frequent rain, though less than in Mumbai, and the winters are mild, so furniture faces far less heat stress than in a Gurugram summer.",
    tip="If you are joining a company in Hinjewadi or Chakan, look at flats in Wakad, Baner or Pimple Saudagar first and fix the address before the survey. A firm Pune address lets us check the society rules and plan the unloading day properly.",
    faqs=[("How many days does Gurugram to Pune shifting take?","Plan for 5 to 7 days on a shared truck from loading. A dedicated truck can reach in 3 to 4 days at a higher price. The coordinator shares the driver's number on the loading day so you can follow the trip."),
          ("Can students move from Gurugram to Pune at a low cost?","Yes. A hostel or PG load of a bed, a desk, a bike and a few cartons is charged as a 1 RK, about Rs 13,000 to 23,000 plus GST on this route. Students who can wait a few extra days for a part load usually pay close to the lower figure."),
          ("Can you shift a small Gurugram office to Pune?","Yes. An office of up to 10 workstations costs about Rs 40,000 to 70,000 and a medium office of 10 to 30 workstations about Rs 80,000 to 1,50,000 on this route, plus GST. An office bigger than 30 desks needs a site visit before we give a figure.")],
    photos=["sp/sp-home-packing-720", "crew/crew-mattress-corrugated", "crew/crew-carton-shoulder", "crew/crew-wrapped-furniture"],
    more=[
     ("Who takes the Gurugram to Pune route", [
       "Pune has become a natural next step for many people working in Gurugram. IT staff move to campuses in Hinjewadi and Kharadi, engineers from the Manesar automotive belt find roles in the Chakan and Talegaon plants, and students head to Pune's colleges with a room's worth of goods. Retired parents also follow children who have settled there. Because the reasons are so mixed, loads on this route range from a single room to a full 4 BHK.",
       "Many families on this route are leaving a builder floor in Palam Vihar, Sushant Lok or one of the HUDA sectors and moving into a new tower in Pune. That means the packing in Gurugram is about narrow stairs, while the unloading in Pune is about lift slots and security gates. Knowing both ends at survey time helps the coordinator decide the crew size at each city and avoid a second visit. It also tells us whether the Pune society allows the truck inside the gate or only up to the road."]),
     ("Getting the timing right for a Pune move", [
       "School admissions in Pune open well before the academic year, so families with children usually aim to move in April or May. That is also the hottest part of the year on the Rajasthan and Madhya Pradesh stretch, so loading is done early in the morning and polished furniture is wrapped twice. Moves in December and January are cooler, but fog on NH48 near Jaipur can slow the first night of driving.",
       "For job moves, the useful rule is to book the truck as soon as the offer letter arrives and the Pune flat is fixed. Shared trucks on this route fill quickly at the end of each month, when many leases end. A booking made two weeks ahead usually gets the date you want, and a confirmed date makes it easier to book the society lift at both ends. If the Pune lease starts on the first of the month, aim to load in Gurugram three or four days before."]),
     ("Gurugram to Pune shifting charges by home size", [
       "On the 500 to 1,500 km band, a 1 BHK from Gurugram to Pune costs about Rs 15,000 to 27,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 20,000 to 36,000, a 3 BHK about Rs 26,000 to 46,000 and a 4 BHK about Rs 34,000 to 58,000, plus GST. A hatchback on a carrier costs about Rs 9,000 to 15,000 plus GST and a compact SUV about Rs 12,000 to 19,000 plus GST. A survey turns the band into one written figure, and that figure is what you pay at delivery."])]),
   dict(key="hyderabad", to="Hyderabad", km=1560, days="6 to 8 days", road="NH44",
    intro="Gurugram to Hyderabad shifting is driven by the growth of HITEC City and the Financial District, where many NCR-based tech, pharma and banking staff now take new roles.",
    about="From Gurugram the truck reaches NH44 at Palwal by the KMP Expressway and stays on that highway almost to the door. It passes Mathura, Agra, Gwalior and Jhansi, crosses Madhya Pradesh through Sagar and Seoni to Nagpur, then enters Telangana through Adilabad, Nirmal and Kamareddy before reaching Hyderabad's Outer Ring Road. The distance is about 1,560 km, just over the 1,500 km mark, so this move is priced in the 1,500 km plus band. A shared truck usually delivers in 6 to 8 days from loading.",
    dest="Most new Hyderabad addresses for people from Gurugram are in the western IT belt: Gachibowli, Kondapur, Nanakramguda, Kokapet and Narsingi. Many of these are large gated communities with tall towers, so the move-in routine is close to what you knew in Gurugram, with an association form, ID proof and a booked lift. Summer in Hyderabad is hot from March to May and the rains come from June to September. The Outer Ring Road makes access to the western suburbs easier for trucks, but city traffic still decides the unloading hour.",
    tip="If you will keep your car in Hyderabad for more than a year, ask about re-registration in Telangana before you leave. Keeping the registration certificate, insurance and pollution papers in one folder makes the later paperwork much simpler.",
    faqs=[("How long does it take to shift from Gurugram to Hyderabad?","Usually 6 to 8 days on a shared truck from loading. A dedicated vehicle is quicker. The coordinator gives you the driver's number and updates you if fog or traffic changes the expected date."),
          ("What does it cost to move a car from Gurugram to Hyderabad?","On a carrier, a hatchback costs about Rs 13,000 to 22,000, a sedan about Rs 15,000 to 25,000, an SUV or MUV about Rs 20,000 to 34,000 and a luxury car in an enclosed carrier about Rs 40,000 to 65,000, plus GST."),
          ("Can you deliver to Secunderabad or the eastern suburbs?","Yes. Delivery anywhere in Hyderabad, including Secunderabad, Uppal and LB Nagar, uses the same 1,500 km plus chart. The partner team at the Hyderabad end plans the unloading time around the local traffic.")],
    photos=["sp/sp-loading-720", "crew/crew-mattress-corrugated", "crew/crew-carton-packing-home", "crew/crew-carton-taping"],
    more=[
     ("Why Gurugram families move to Hyderabad", [
       "Global companies have opened large offices in Hyderabad's Financial District and HITEC City, and many of the people they hire come from the NCR. A manager at a Gurugram MNC may be asked to lead a new team in Gachibowli, or an analyst may simply find a better offer there. Lower rents in the western suburbs compared with Golf Course Road also tempt families to take a bigger home. Pharmaceutical and life sciences jobs add another group, often moving with young children.",
       "For Gurugram to Hyderabad packers and movers, the common load is a 2 BHK or 3 BHK from a society in Sector 56, Sohna Road or the Dwarka Expressway, plus one car. Because Hyderabad homes are often larger, people tend to bring everything rather than sell, so the survey count of furniture and appliances matters. A clear list helps the coordinator pick the right truck size and keeps the estimate close to the final bill."]),
     ("Packing for the heat on the central highway", [
       "The NH44 run through Madhya Pradesh and Vidarbha can be very hot from April to June, and the truck carries the goods through that heat for several days. Wax candles, cosmetics and medicines should travel with you, not in the truck. Refrigerators are defrosted and dried the day before, washing machines are drained and their drums locked, and televisions go into thick foam or their original boxes. Air conditioners taken down from a Gurugram flat travel with their outdoor units padded and the copper pipes capped.",
       "Wooden furniture is wrapped in corrugated sheet and film so that dust does not settle in the joints. Mattresses are bagged, and sofas are covered on all sides. Each carton is labelled with the room it belongs to in the new house, which saves a lot of time when the Hyderabad team unloads into a large flat. The inventory sheet is signed at both ends, so any damage claim has a clear record. Gas cylinders are not carried in the household truck, so return or transfer the connection before you leave Gurugram."]),
     ("Gurugram to Hyderabad shifting charges", [
       "At about 1,560 km, a 1 BHK from Gurugram to Hyderabad costs about Rs 20,000 to 35,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 27,000 to 47,000 and a 3 BHK about Rs 34,000 to 60,000, plus GST. A small office of up to 10 workstations costs about Rs 55,000 to 90,000 plus GST. A scooter costs about Rs 4,500 to 7,000 plus GST and a premium bike above 350cc about Rs 10,000 to 14,500 plus GST. Insurance and any storage are separate lines on the estimate."])]),
   dict(key="chennai", to="Chennai", km=2170, days="7 to 9 days", road="NH44 and NH16",
    intro="This route mostly carries IT, automotive and manufacturing professionals bound for OMR and the industrial belt, and families from Tamil Nadu returning home after years in the NCR.",
    about="This is one of the longest routes from Gurugram. The truck joins NH44 at Palwal and runs south through Agra, Gwalior, Jhansi and Nagpur into Telangana, then heads south-east to the Andhra coast near Vijayawada and takes NH16 south through Ongole and Nellore into Chennai. The total is about 2,170 km, so this move falls in the 1,500 km plus band, the top band of our rate card. On a shared truck household goods usually arrive in 7 to 9 days from the day of loading.",
    dest="Chennai is hot and humid for much of the year, and its main rainy season is the northeast monsoon from October to December, when heavy downpours can waterlog low-lying roads in Velachery, Pallikaranai and parts of OMR. That is the opposite of Gurugram's July rains, so people are often caught out. Apartment complexes along OMR and in Porur and Medavakkam ask for an association form and a lift slot, while older homes in Mylapore, T Nagar and Anna Nagar may have narrow stairs and limited parking for the truck.",
    tip="Avoid a Chennai unloading date in the middle of a cyclone warning between October and December. If one is forecast, the coordinator holds the truck at a safe stop and delivers once the roads are clear.",
    faqs=[("How long does shifting from Gurugram to Chennai take?","Plan for 7 to 9 days on a shared truck from loading. In winter, fog in the north can slow the first stretch, and in the northeast monsoon rain in Andhra Pradesh and Tamil Nadu can slow the last one. You are told early if the date moves."),
          ("Can you send my bike from Gurugram to Chennai?","Yes. A scooter costs about Rs 4,500 to 7,000, a bike up to 150cc about Rs 5,000 to 7,500, a 150cc to 350cc bike about Rs 7,000 to 10,000 and a superbike in a crate about Rs 18,000 to 28,000 on this route, plus GST."),
          ("How do you protect goods from Chennai's humidity?","Wooden furniture is wrapped in corrugated sheet and stretch film, steel almirahs and appliances are packed with extra corner padding, and clothes and books go in plastic-lined cartons. Once unloaded, open the cartons within a few days so nothing stays sealed in damp air.")],
    photos=["sp/sp-loading-720", "crew/crew-mattress-corrugated", "crew/crew-carton-packing-home", "crew/crew-carton-shoulder"],
    more=[
     ("Who moves from Gurugram to Chennai", [
       "Chennai draws Gurugram professionals in several ways. IT and back-office staff move to campuses on OMR, in Siruseri and around Guindy. Engineers from the Manesar and Gurugram auto industry find roles in the car and component plants on the Sriperumbudur and Oragadam side. And many families from Tamil Nadu who spent ten or fifteen years in the NCR decide to go home as children reach college age or parents need care.",
       "Returning families usually bring a full house, sometimes with furniture bought over many years, so the survey has to be thorough. Younger professionals tend to move a 1 BHK and a bike. Either way, home shifting from Gurugram to Chennai goes smoothly when the move-in date at the new flat is fixed first, because a truck arriving early at a Chennai complex with no lift slot booked can wait half a day at the gate. The coordinator confirms the slot with the Chennai association before the truck leaves Gurugram."]),
     ("Planning a 2,170 km move", [
       "A move of this length needs more planning than a city shift. Book the truck two to three weeks ahead, fix the Chennai address before the survey and keep a small bag of essentials with you for the first week, since the goods arrive several days after you do. If you are flying, give a trusted person the keys and the inventory list in Gurugram in case the loading slot moves.",
       "Furniture with glass, marble table tops and large mirrors are crated or packed between boards for this distance. Electronics are packed in foam, and the serial numbers of expensive items are noted on the inventory sheet. If the new home is not ready, storage can be arranged through a partner warehouse, charged separately and shown on the estimate, with the goods delivered when you are ready. Ask for this at the survey so it is priced in from the start."]),
     ("Gurugram to Chennai shifting charges explained", [
       "For about 2,170 km, a 1 RK from Gurugram to Chennai costs about Rs 18,000 to 32,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 27,000 to 47,000, a 3 BHK about Rs 34,000 to 60,000 and a 4 BHK about Rs 44,000 to 78,000, plus GST. A sedan on a carrier costs about Rs 15,000 to 25,000 plus GST and a compact SUV about Rs 17,000 to 28,000 plus GST. A medium office of 10 to 30 workstations costs about Rs 1,10,000 to 2,00,000 plus GST. Tolls and insurance are shown as separate lines."])]),
   dict(key="kolkata", to="Kolkata", km=1550, days="6 to 8 days", road="NH44 and NH19",
    intro="This route carries a steady flow of Bengali families returning home, as well as finance, IT and FMCG staff transferred to Salt Lake and New Town.",
    about="Trucks from Gurugram usually reach Palwal on the KMP Expressway and follow NH44 to Agra, where NH19, the old Grand Trunk Road, begins. That highway runs east past Etawah, Kanpur, Prayagraj and Varanasi, crosses Bihar through Sasaram and Aurangabad, and enters Bengal past Dhanbad and Asansol before Durgapur and Kolkata. The distance is about 1,550 km, so the move sits in the 1,500 km plus band of our chart. A shared truck usually takes 6 to 8 days from loading, with fog in winter the main cause of delay.",
    dest="Kolkata has two very different kinds of homes. New Town, Rajarhat and the newer parts of Salt Lake have tall towers with lifts and society rules much like Gurugram's. Older homes in north and south Kolkata, from Shyambazar to Behala, are often in old buildings with steep stairs and no lift, on lanes too narrow for a big truck, so the last part of the delivery is done in a smaller vehicle. The city is humid all year and the monsoon runs from June to September. During Durga Puja in September or October many roads are closed for pandals, so unloading then needs extra planning.",
    tip="Do not plan a Kolkata unloading in the main Durga Puja days if you can avoid it. Road closures and crowds make access slow, and some housing societies do not allow moves during the festival.",
    faqs=[("How long does Gurugram to Kolkata shifting take?","Usually 6 to 8 days on a shared truck from the loading day. In December and January, fog on the plains of Uttar Pradesh and Bihar can add a day or two, and the coordinator tells you as soon as the plan changes."),
          ("Can you move an office from Gurugram to Kolkata?","Yes. A small office of up to 10 workstations costs about Rs 55,000 to 90,000 and a medium office of 10 to 30 workstations about Rs 1,10,000 to 2,00,000 on this route, plus GST. For more than 30 workstations, we visit the office first and then quote."),
          ("Can goods be delivered to Howrah or the northern suburbs?","Yes. Howrah, Dum Dum, Baranagar and the other suburbs use the same 1,500 km plus chart as central Kolkata. If the lane is narrow, the partner team transfers goods to a smaller vehicle for the last stretch.")],
    photos=["sp/sp-home-packing-720", "crew/crew-paper-wrap-taping", "crew/crew-carton-shoulder", "crew/crew-carton-taping"],
    more=[
     ("Who shifts from Gurugram to Kolkata", [
       "Many people on this route are going home. Bengali families who moved to Gurugram for work often return to Kolkata to be near parents, to buy a flat at a lower price or to put children in schools they know. Others are moving the other way in their careers: bank, FMCG and IT staff transferred to offices in Salt Lake Sector V and New Town. Retired couples also send their household back after their children settle elsewhere.",
       "Returning families usually carry a lot of sentimental items, from old wooden almirahs to books and musical instruments such as a harmonium or tabla. These need careful packing, with corrugated sheet and padding at every corner. For Gurugram to Kolkata packers and movers, listing such items at the survey helps us size the truck and put the fragile pieces on the inventory sheet by name. A piano or a large antique may need a crate, which is quoted on the estimate."]),
     ("Packing for Kolkata's humidity and old buildings", [
       "Goods that leave a dry Gurugram winter can arrive in a damp Kolkata, so clothes, books and documents go in plastic-lined cartons, and steel almirahs and appliances get padding at the corners. Leather sofas and wooden furniture are wrapped in film over corrugated sheet. Once unloaded, it helps to open cartons quickly and let things air rather than leaving them sealed for weeks. A few silica gel sachets in boxes of documents and photo albums also help in the first damp weeks.",
       "If the new address is an older building with steep stairs, the partner team takes heavy pieces apart before they go up and sends extra hands for the carry. Where a big truck cannot enter the lane, goods are moved into a smaller vehicle at the main road, and that transfer is shown on the estimate as its own line rather than added on the day. Our coordinator checks the lane on a map or with the partner team before quoting, so this is known in advance."]),
     ("Gurugram to Kolkata shifting charges", [
       "On the 1,500 km plus band, a 1 BHK from Gurugram to Kolkata costs about Rs 20,000 to 35,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 27,000 to 47,000 and a 3 BHK about Rs 34,000 to 60,000, plus GST. A hatchback on a carrier costs about Rs 13,000 to 22,000 plus GST and an SUV or MUV about Rs 20,000 to 34,000 plus GST. A bike up to 150cc costs about Rs 5,000 to 7,500 plus GST. The written figure after the survey is the final price, with GST shown."])]),
  ],
)

